# Car Wash Station Conversion implementation Plan

This document outlines the systematic plan to convert the existing Barbershop Queue SaaS application into a Car Wash Station Queue application, based on the user's requirements.

## Goal Description
Transform the application from a multi-barber queuing system to a single-pipeline car wash queue. This involves removing all "barber" related concepts, employee selection, and the TV display feature. The ticketing will be sequential (1, 2, 3...) for the entire station, and the whole design will be revamped to reflect a car wash theme.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Database & Types (Supabase)
We will update the database schema and TypeScript interfaces to reflect the single queue.

#### [MODIFY] [supabase/schema.sql](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/Downloads/Kimi_Agent_Barbershop%20Queue%20SaaS%20PRD%20%281%29/lavageticket/supabase/schema.sql)
- Remove the `barbers` table.
- Remove `barber_id` from the `tickets` table.
- Update `create_ticket` RPC: Remove `p_barber_id` parameter; simplify the `hashtext` advisory lock to just `p_shop_id`; calculate `v_next_num` based on the shop's total tickets for the day instead of partitioning by barber.
- Update `get_people_ahead` RPC: Remove `p_barber_id` parameter; calculate sum of `people_count` for all waiting tickets in the shop before `p_created_at`.
- Update `process_next_customer` RPC: Remove `p_barber_id` parameter; fetch the first available ticket in the shop and mark it as `serving`.
- Update `get_next_ticket_number` RPC (if exists standalone): Remove `p_barber_id`.
- Remove `get_queue_status_public` (used for TV).

#### [MODIFY] [src/types/database.ts](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/Downloads/Kimi_Agent_Barbershop%20Queue%20SaaS%20PRD%20%281%29/lavageticket/src/types/database.ts)
- Remove the [Barber](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/Downloads/Kimi_Agent_Barbershop%20Queue%20SaaS%20PRD%20%281%29/lavageticket/src/types/database.ts#58-66) interface.
- Remove `barber_id` from the [Ticket](file:///c:/Users/ADMIN/Downloads/Kimi_Agent_Barbershop%20Queue%20SaaS%20PRD%20%281%29/lavageticket/src/types/database.ts#67-80) interface.
- Update the arguments and return types of `Tables` and `Functions` to match the new SQL schema.

